WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.002
-Michael, this is your
late-night-TV debut.

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:05.070
-This is it. This is it.
-I'm very excited. This is --

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.973
[ Cheers and applause ]
-It's like one of things.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.241
Like, I'm a little nervous.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.909
But I was saying it's one of
those things that, like,

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.644
you talk about it
in acting school.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:14.180
It's like, "One day,
we're going to be here."

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.915
So it's pretty --
it's pretty wild.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:18.551
So thank you. Thank you.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:22.221
-I'm honored to have you here
and that we're your first show.

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:25.358
You play Tony Soprano
in this new movie.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.894
And before --
I want to go back to --

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:28.961
'cause when you were
in high school,

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:30.964
you did play another
iconic character.

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.265
-I did, yes. Yeah.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:35.101
-In theater acting,
you were Shrek in high school.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.403
-I was, yeah.
-And this is you.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:38.905
-There you go.
-Now, that's --

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:41.007
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:44.577
-Yeah, yeah.
-This is prosthetics.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.513
What do you remember about
getting in these prosthetics?

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:52.986
-Well, you know, I was working
with a makeup artist named Linda

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:56.856
and I had to convince my
history teacher to let me

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.492
out of class to be able to go
and sit in the chair

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.327
for two hours before the show.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.796
-That's kind of amazing
for high school.

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.498
-But my school, at first,
had a very different

00:01:06.498 --> 00:01:08.801
idea of makeup, so...

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:10.803
-Yeah, you brought us
a picture of what you were

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:12.771
originally going to be
looking like as Shrek.

00:01:12.771 --> 00:01:14.840
Now, again,
this is a play for children.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.176
-Yeah, it is, it is, in my
school, so --

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:19.612
-Here's the original makeup
test for Shrek.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.013
-Yeah.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:23.850
Yeah, that was -- Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.853
[ Tuba plays sad note ]
-Oh, my God!

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.121
That's frightening.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.690
Yeah, I couldn't --
I remember not being able --

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.260
They stuffed a jacket behind,
and my eyes were, like,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.563
pushing forward, and I couldn't
see anything onstage.

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:40.165
And they would, like, have me
run around and sing, like,

00:01:40.165 --> 00:01:42.702
these Shrek songs,
and I would run into walls.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:43.903
-That is so scary.
-It was, yeah.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:46.372
-Imagine if that
ever showed up in a window

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.473
in the middle of the night.

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:48.974
"Whoa!"

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:50.710
Gosh!
-Exactly.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.080
-But someone saw you when
you were doing this version

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.281
and said,
"Hey, I want to work with you.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.281
I think you got something, kid."

00:01:56.281 --> 00:01:57.850
-Yeah, it's very true.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.453
That play was the first thing
that got me a manager,

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.955
and then that manager
had me audition,

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.124
and now we're here, yeah.

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:08.561
-I want to you talk about this,
'cause I knew your dad.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.297
He was a great guy to me.
He was so funny.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.831
He was Tony Soprano.
-Yeah.

00:02:12.831 --> 00:02:16.202
-I mean, that's --
And "The Sopranos to you --

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.271
did it mean anything
or you were just a kid

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.605
just playing around on set?

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:23.109
-I mean, yeah, the show was,
like, a jungle gym to me.

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.011
Like, that's sort of
what I knew.

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:29.615
I had grown up on the set,
but set to me was, you know,

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:31.618
being, you know,
in my dad's trailer.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.685
And Tony Soprano
was no more than, like,

00:02:33.685 --> 00:02:35.521
my dad eating a sandwich
in a robe.

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:37.223
Like, I didn't --
-That's -- Yeah.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.290
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:40.392
-Here's a picture of you on set

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:42.495
with your dad and Edie
in the background.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.796
-Yeah.
-And look at you.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:46.466
I mean, I got to --
It's got to be bizarre.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:49.835
a full circle of craziness that
you're playing that role,

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:52.471
a younger version of what your
dad played, Tony Soprano.

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:54.773
-It's -- I mean,
it's incredible.

00:02:54.773 --> 00:02:56.508
You know, full circle.

00:02:56.508 --> 00:02:58.978
And to have gotten
to work with Vera and Jon

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:01.814
and Alessandro and Leslie, like,
the caliber of actors

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.083
as a young actor.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.417
But it was surreal.

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:08.988
And the fact that David sort of
trusted me to play Tony,

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.856
which is one of
the greatest characters,

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:12.625
you know, like --

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.760
-Were you hesitant at all to go
like, "Well, look, I get it.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:15.762
I understand.

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:16.962
But, no, I don't want to do this

00:03:16.962 --> 00:03:18.231
because it's my dad,
and I don't want to --"

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:19.465
-Yeah, completely.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:23.469
I thought -- Not only
because of, you know,

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.538
I want to be my own actor,
my own person,

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:28.608
but, also, I didn't --
I had never seen the show.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:30.476
So I didn't even know
what Tony was.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:31.477
I was like --
-You've never -- Really?

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.913
-No, no.
-You've never watched it?

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.014
Well, of course not.
It's not really for kids.

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.917
-Yeah, yeah. I was little.
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.318
So...
-You have to watch it.

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:40.553
It's a great show.
-No, I've seen it now.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:41.954
-Oh, okay. I'm sorry.
Okay, yeah, okay.

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:43.122
I was like, "Wow!

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:44.390
Get ready, 'cause you're gonna
be blown --

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.925
Your dad was really amazing."

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.493
-I mean, that would
have been insane

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.862
just going in blind, just like,
"I don't know, we'll see."

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.798
-"I've never seen it.
Is a comedy? Let's do it."

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:55.768
-Yeah, no, I watched the
first season during my --

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.903
during the audition process,
and I was just like,

00:03:57.903 --> 00:04:00.106
"I'll stay with
the first season."

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:02.341
And then I went on and on
and then, you know,

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:05.344
I became a fan of the show
like everyone else.

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:06.446
I just loved it.

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:08.013
-I think you did
such a great job.

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:09.748
And, I mean, you would know
better than me,

00:04:09.748 --> 00:04:12.751
but your dad's got to be smiling
at you and so proud of you.

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:14.453
-Thank you.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:17.557
Here's Michael Gandolfini in
"The Many Saints of Newark."

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:18.790
Take a look.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.393
-I want to go to college.

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:21.961
I can't get [bleep] like this.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.896
-Hey, my friend Hess

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:27.266
says only goys and children
pay retail.

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:33.138
-This isn't wholesale.
It's totally on the arm.

00:04:33.138 --> 00:04:36.108
-Look, you want to be
a civilian.

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:38.777
I appreciate that.
I'm all for it.

00:04:38.777 --> 00:04:40.980
But pay attention to me
for once, okay?

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.815
You take the speakers, right?

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:44.951
At the same time,
you promise yourself,

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.318
"These speakers are it.

00:04:46.318 --> 00:04:48.387
Now, you say to yourself,
"This is the last time

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:52.025
I'm ever going to steal
something," and you stick to it.

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:56.062
It's that simple.

00:05:03.036 --> 00:05:05.237
-Yeah!
That's what I'm talking about.

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:07.306
Michael Gandolfini, everybody!

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:10.042
"The Many Saints of Newark"
is in theaters

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:12.879
and streaming on HBO Max
starting Friday.

